  "summary": "This phase II trial studies the effects of binimetinib and encorafenib in treating patients with melanoma that has spread to the central nervous system (metastases). Binimetinib and encorafenib may stop the growth of tumor cells by blocking some of the enzymes needed for cell growth. Giving binimetinib and encorafenib may help control melanoma that has spread to the brain.",
  "title": "Binimetinib and Encorafenib for the Treatment of Metastatic Melanoma and Central Nervous System Metastases"
